Subject: Cantor M2B Windows Sys Direct Feature and ABI Compile Probe Justification

& [JustificationIdentity] is the dependency-proof rationale
  + [justification_uuid] is 5162f513-d2d1-48a5-a593-52680c925501
  + [solution_uuid] is 500dfdff-fee7-4c38-bcdd-af5ea25522bf
  + [status] is implementation_justified

! [PrimaryClaim] Cantor should own and compile the exact generated Windows dependency surface before any runtime seam is designed
  @ [support] windows-sys 0.61.2 is already locked and transitively feature-enabled
  @ [support] generated CreateFileW requires the Security feature while file structures require Storage_FileSystem
  @ [support] a test-only no-call probe can prove availability without opening a physical effect boundary
  + [confidence] is high for dependency and generated-symbol availability on the current toolchain
  + [confidence_limit] is none for runtime API success, filesystem support, or scanner correctness

& [WhyDirectDependency] is ownership
  + [current_weakness] Cantor compiles only because mio and tokio currently request overlapping features
  + [future_risk] transitive dependency changes can remove Cantor's undeclared API prerequisites
  + [repair] exact target dependency makes the contract reviewable and stable under Cargo resolution

& [WhyTestOnly] is authority minimization
  + [need] prove names, features, structures, class values, and constants are available
  + [no_need] no production caller or wrapper is required for that proof
  + [benefit] compiler and linker check generated declarations while no path, handle, or API invocation exists

& [WhyNoCall] is a semantic boundary
  + [availability] function-item resolution proves generated and linked surface availability
  + [invocation] would create OS interaction, error classification, pointer, ownership, and physical proof obligations
  + [decision] invocation remains a separately sourced M2C boundary

& [Counterarguments] are resolved
  + [keep_transitive] is rejected because implicit dependency contracts are fragile and unreviewable
  + [add_all_features] is rejected because broad feature surface obscures the minimum seam
  + [write_wrapper_now] is rejected because unsafe, ownership, and physical evidence gates remain locked
  + [only_read_generated_source] is insufficient because source inspection does not prove Cantor's Cargo target and linker configuration
  + [cross_platform_claim] is rejected because the focused probe measures the current Windows target only

& [InvalidationConditions] are explicit
  + [package_change] is windows-sys version, source, checksum, license, or generated module change
  + [feature_change] is any addition, removal, default activation, or transitive-only reliance
  + [lock_change] is any Cargo.lock byte change
  + [probe_change] is call expression, unsafe token, production export, or external input
  + [verification_failure] is focused, global, static, audit, evidence, or registry failure
  = must: stop and reprocess rather than expand authority

& [Tradeoff] favors narrow redundant declaration
  + [cost] one direct dependency declaration duplicates a package already in the graph
  + [benefit] no new package while Cantor's own feature contract becomes explicit
  + [maintenance] exact version requires deliberate re-review on upgrade

& [Rollback] is trivial
  + [action] remove target dependency table and Windows-only integration test
  + [lock] remains unchanged
  + [migration] is none
